00:05:14.086 --> 00:05:15.963
Core Concepts, Beginner to Deep.

88
00:05:17.213 --> 00:05:20.157
Intuition: the shop's ledger and its photocopies.

89
00:05:20.437 --> 00:05:23.232
The shop owner keeps the master ledger (the leader).

90
00:05:23.512 --> 00:05:28.973
Every evening an assistant photocopies the day's pages for the branch office (an async follower).

91
00:05:29.253 --> 00:05:34.053
If the branch reads the photocopy at 6 pm, it's missing the afternoon's sales.

92
00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:35.827
That's replication lag.

93
00:05:36.107 --> 00:05:41.248
If the shop burns down at 5 pm, today's sales since yesterday's copy are lost.

94
00:05:41.528 --> 00:05:43.875
That's the RPO of async replication.

95
00:05:45.225 --> 00:05:58.238
If the owner insists the assistant copy each page before the owner moves on (sync replication), nothing is lost, but the owner waits for the assistant, and if the assistant is out sick the owner can't write at all.

96
00:05:58.518 --> 00:06:08.673
If the branch decides the shop has burned down (it hasn't; the phone line is cut) and starts its own ledger, there are now two ledgers accepting sales: a split brain.

