566
00:32:09.710 --> 00:32:10.777
Calculation:

567
00:32:11.057 --> 00:32:14.577
Group commit amortizes the waits; commits run concurrently.

568
00:32:14.857 --> 00:32:15.667
Result:

569
00:32:15.947 --> 00:32:18.763
Negligible at ~1.4 K per second.

570
00:32:19.043 --> 00:32:20.473
WAL volume.

571
00:32:20.753 --> 00:32:25.958
Calculation: ~2 to 4 MB per second at peak (Ch 05).

572
00:32:26.238 --> 00:32:27.049
Result:

573
00:32:27.329 --> 00:32:32.555
Cross-AZ traffic ~250 GB per day per standby: a cost line.

574
00:32:32.835 --> 00:32:33.731
RTO.

575
00:32:34.011 --> 00:32:40.966
Calculation: ttl 30 s + promotion ~2 s + endpoint update ~5 s.

576
00:32:41.246 --> 00:32:42.889
Result: ~40 s.

577
00:32:44.239 --> 00:32:46.009
Async DR standby lag.

578
00:32:46.289 --> 00:32:47.356
Calculation:

579
00:32:47.636 --> 00:32:50.537
Cross-region, ~60 ms RTT.

580
00:32:50.817 --> 00:32:51.628
Result:

581
00:32:51.908 --> 00:32:56.068
RPO seconds for region loss (accepted, Ch 27).

582
00:32:57.418 --> 00:32:58.186
5.

583
00:32:58.466 --> 00:32:59.661
Proposed design.

584
00:32:59.941 --> 00:33:08.581
Patroni-managed PostgreSQL: a primary and two standbys in three AZs, with synchronousmode: true and synchronousnodecount:

585
00:33:08.861 --> 00:33:18.034
1 (Patroni maintains ANY 1 (...)), synchronousmodestrict: false (see §7 for the trade-off), and an async DR standby in another region.

586
00:33:19.384 --> 00:33:24.973
Durability per transaction: money-class transactions run with synchronouscommit = on.

587
00:33:25.253 --> 00:33:33.808
Low-value writes (audit trails that are also in Kafka, analytics counters) run with SET LOCAL synchronouscommit = local.

588
00:33:34.088 --> 00:33:41.192
A client timeout during the sync wait is an unknown outcome, handled by idempotent retry (Ch 04).

589
00:33:41.472 --> 00:33:42.325
Fencing:

590
00:33:42.605 --> 00:33:53.848
DCS lease (etcd), self-demotion, Linux softdog watchdog (watchdog: mode: required), and a single writer endpoint (the Patroni-maintained Kubernetes Service).

591
00:33:54.128 --> 00:33:56.197
Pods never connect to node IPs.

592
00:33:57.547 --> 00:33:58.635
Replica reads:

593
00:33:58.915 --> 00:34:03.630
ReplicaSelector with a session token = max LSN written or read.

594
00:34:03.910 --> 00:34:06.875
Replicas lagging more than 16 MB are skipped.

595
00:34:07.155 --> 00:34:19.379
After every failover: pgrewind the old primary and any standby that followed it after the fork, and run FailoverReconciler over the window failure minus 5 min, failover + 5 min.

596
00:34:19.659 --> 00:34:20.406
