00:46:02.094 --> 00:46:03.737
Which exceptions mean unknown.

748
00:46:04.017 --> 00:46:12.486
Only failures that can happen after COMMIT was sent are truly ambiguous (a timeout or connection loss while waiting for the commit response).

749
00:46:12.766 --> 00:46:18.974
A constraint violation or a timeout during an earlier statement means the transaction did not commit.

750
00:46:19.254 --> 00:46:27.574
Keep the mapping narrow, and pair every money-class write with an idempotency key, so a retry after an unknown outcome is always safe.

